<h2>Where should the filter controls go on Account activity?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Wireframes only. Each one shows an Event select, a Search field and a polite result count above or around the existing table. Click the one you prefer.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div style="padding:12px;font-size:12px">
        <div style="font-weight:600">Account activity</div>
        <div style="color:#666;margin-bottom:8px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-end;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px">
          <div><div style="font-size:11px">Event</div><div class="mock-input" style="width:110px">All events ▾</div></div>
          <div><div style="font-size:11px">Search</div><div class="mock-input" style="width:150px">Device, location, details</div></div>
        </div>
        <div style="color:#666;margin-bottom:6px">Showing 52 of 52 events</div>
        <div class="placeholder" style="height:70px">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A. Inline filter bar above the table</h3>
      <p>Labels above controls, wraps to a stack at 320px. Simplest markup; controls always visible.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div style="padding:12px;font-size:12px">
        <div style="font-weight:600">Account activity</div>
        <div style="color:#666;margin-bottom:8px">Every sign-in and account change ...</div>
        <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px">
          <tr style="background:#eee"><td>When</td><td>Event</td><td>Device</td><td>Location</td><td>IP</td><td>Details</td></tr>
          <tr style="background:#f6f6f6"><td></td><td><span class="mock-input" style="padding:1px 4px">All ▾</span></td><td><span class="mock-input" style="padding:1px 4px">...</span></td><td><span class="mock-input" style="padding:1px 4px">...</span></td><td></td><td><span class="mock-input" style="padding:1px 4px">...</span></td></tr>
        </table>
        <div class="placeholder" style="height:60px;margin-top:4px">Rows</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B. Filter row inside the table header</h3>
      <p>Per-column filters. Compact, but hard to label properly and breaks reflow at 320px.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div style="padding:12px;font-size:12px">
        <div style="font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px">Account activity</div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px">
          <div class="mock-sidebar" style="width:90px;font-size:11px">
            Event<br><span class="mock-input" style="display:block">All ▾</span><br>
            Search<br><span class="mock-input" style="display:block">...</span>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder" style="flex:1;height:110px">Table (narrower)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>C. Left rail</h3>
      <p>Room for more filters later, but squeezes a six-column table in a 960px page.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="d" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div style="padding:12px;font-size:12px">
        <div style="font-weight:600">Account activity</div>
        <div style="color:#666;margin-bottom:8px">Every sign-in and account change ...</div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:6px">
          <button class="mock-button" style="font-size:11px">Filter</button>
          <span style="font-size:11px;border:1px solid #99c;border-radius:10px;padding:1px 6px">Sign-in failed ✕</span>
        </div>
        <div class="placeholder" style="height:80px">Table</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>D. Filter button opening a popover</h3>
      <p>Tidy, with applied filters as removable tags. Extra click to find failed sign-ins; more focus management.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
